<td id="S5.T3.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S5.T3.2.8.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">0.024</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><math id="S5.T3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.068" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0.068</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.068</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T3.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T3.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S5.T3.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">judge_entailment</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S5.T3.2.9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">0.434</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S5.T3.2.9.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">0.183</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><math id="S5.T3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{-0.250}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="bold">0.250</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{-0.250}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Selecting on tune-set <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> alone would have identified the two-pass entailment judge as the headline signal at the cost of doubling per-round LLM calls, but the held-out split reveals its separation collapses by <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25</annotation></semantics></math>. The stability of <span id="S5.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">answer_stable</span> reflects the structure of trajectory convergence rather than a dataset-specific artifact: once a model repeats an answer across consecutive retrieval rounds, that agreement is a direct convergence indicator. This generalizes across models: AS_m25 achieves eval <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.55</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.00</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.00</annotation></semantics></math> across all three models, with tune-to-eval drift <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 0.09" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.09</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 0.09</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.6. </span>External validity: open-domain BM25 corpora</h3>

<div id="S5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To test whether TASR generalizes beyond the curated distractor pool, we re-run the identical pipeline on nine open-domain cells using Pyserini Lucene indexes, with calibration locked from each model’s HotpotQA-distractor tune split. Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 5.6. External validity: open-domain BM25 corpora ‣ 5. Results ‣ TASR: Training-Free Adaptive Stopping for Iterative Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> reports the results.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4. </span>Open-domain BM25 results (<math id="S5.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math> eval Qs/cell). Calibration locked from distractor tune split. <math id="S5.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>F1 &amp; CIs: paired bootstrap (<math id="S5.T4.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1{,}000\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1,000</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000\times</annotation></semantics></math>, seed <math id="S5.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="42" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>42</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">42</annotation></semantics></math>) vs. <math id="S5.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
