</figure>
<div id="S5.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The distractor-grid pattern is preserved: TASR matches fixed-<math id="S5.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> F1 at matched cost and approaches fixed-<math id="S5.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}5</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S5.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40\%</annotation></semantics></math> fewer calls. Six of nine cells show TASR <math id="S5.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq</annotation></semantics></math> fixed-<math id="S5.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>; the three cells with small regressions are devstral_nq (<math id="S5.SS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.81" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.81</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.81</annotation></semantics></math>), devstral_trivia (<math id="S5.SS6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.84" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.84</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.84</annotation></semantics></math>, a tie), and gemma_trivia (<math id="S5.SS6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.06" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.06</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.06</annotation></semantics></math>). The open-domain results are notable because the calibration is <em id="S5.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">transferred</em>: per-model isotonic regression is fit once on each model’s HotpotQA-distractor tune split and applied unchanged to entirely different corpora (fullwiki, NQ-Open, TriviaQA-Open). No per-corpus tuning is performed. The fact that a single calibration transfer preserves the Pareto pattern suggests that the margin-to-correctness mapping is a property of the model rather than the corpus.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.7. </span>Retriever robustness: dense retrieval, two families</h3>

<div id="S5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To rule out that TASR’s signal is BM25-specific, we re-run all three open-domain corpora with dense retrievers and locked calibration:
<span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contriever-MSMARCO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Izacard et al., 2022</a>)</cite> on HotpotQA-fullwiki and NQ-Open, and <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DKRR-TQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Izacard and Grave, 2021</a>)</cite> on
TriviaQA-Open (DKRR is the standard dense baseline for that corpus, as Contriever has no prebuilt index for wikipedia-dpr-100w). The two families
differ in architecture, training objective, and training corpus.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5. </span>Dense retrieval, <math id="S5.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math> cells across two retriever families. Same <math id="S5.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math> eval Qs/cell; calibration locked from BM25-distractor tune split.
<math id="S5.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>F1 &amp; CIs vs. fixed-<math id="S5.T5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
